We examine the decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ within the $U_1$ leptoquark framework, utilizing recent experimental data from Belle II and LHCb regarding $b 	o c$ transitions. Our findings indicate that precise measurements of $b 	o c$ transitions impose significant constraints on the model parameters, which in turn restrict the predicted branching fraction for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$. Furthermore, we analyze the potential of this decay to probe new physics by comparing the contributions of the leptoquark to those of the Standard Model. We project that future high-precision analyses of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ by Belle II and LHCb could enhance the limits on the $U_1$ leptoquark model.
